Where does entry_id come from here? Look at the function signature: def log_entry(): — no entry_id parameter. This function never received an entry_id from anywhere;
it's creating a brand new entry, so there's no id yet until after you commit.

You actually already worked this out correctly a few turns back — after db.session.commit(), the new row's id becomes available as an attribute on the object you just created.
 What's that object called in this function? Look at your Entry(...) call — what did you name the variable?

Given that, what should replace entry_id=entry_id in that redirect line?

